{"id": "EUVD-2026-27748", "enisaUuid": "02093288-50a3-33bf-888a-e8f8c58c3f4b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix signededness bug in smb_direct_prepare_negotiation()\n\nsmb_direct_prepare_negotiation() casts an unsigned __u32 value\nfrom sp->max_recv_size and req->preferred_send_size to a signed\nint before computing min_t(int, ...). A maliciously provided\npreferred_send_size of 0x80000000 will return as smaller than\nmax_recv_size, and then be used to set the maximum allowed\nalowed receive size for the next message.\n\nBy sending a second message with a large value (>1420 bytes)\nthe attacker can then achieve a heap buffer overflow.\n\nThis fix replaces min_t(int, ...) with min_t(u32)", "datePublished": "2026-05-06T11:27:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:13", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56eab82fa6fb5ca024b0514e249d40d9b23ee5a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a110dbe928561d440e9e117d17331139a0bedace", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ceae058eb707ddd0d68f0872f9d9f23b7c30c37b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/55abc475d096da4a5356b6efb0cfdc6156bc1550", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6b4f875aac344cdd52a1f34cc70ed2f874a65757"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vcg7-gx5w-x44c", "CVE-2026-43185"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.73, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "077f1d5a-0f31-3a80-a15f-b530643fe460", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0626e6641f6b467447c81dd7678a69c66f7746cf <56eab82fa6fb5ca024b0514e249d40d9b23ee5a7"}, {"id": "18c9801c-0f42-38b8-b697-21cd4caaeb8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.6"}, {"id": "25e29393-09be-33b6-841c-32211bbce0f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "457db3c5-19e5-3d88-b90f-40c957de5742", "pr